## 1. System Overview

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        Reporting Host                            │
│                                                                   │
│  ┌──────────────┐   ┌──────────────┐   ┌───────────────────┐   │
│  │ Plugin        │   │ Lifecycle     │   │ Permission         │   │
│  │ Registry      │──▶│ Manager       │──▶│ Broker             │   │
│  └──────────────┘   └──────────────┘   └───────────────────┘   │
│         │                    │                     │            │
│         ▼                    ▼                     ▼            │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │              Host API (versioned, RPC-exposed)             │  │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘  │
└─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┘
                               │ IPC / RPC boundary (JSON-RPC 2.0)
        ┌──────────────────────┼──────────────────────┐
        ▼                      ▼                      ▼
┌───────────────┐     ┌───────────────┐     ┌───────────────┐
│ Plugin Host    │     │ Plugin Host    │     │ Plugin Host    │
│ Process A      │     │ Process B      │     │ Process C      │
│ (data-source)  │     │ (renderer)     │     │ (exporter)     │
│ sandbox        │     │ sandbox        │     │ sandbox        │
└───────────────┘     └───────────────┘     └───────────────┘
```

Each plugin runs in its **own OS process**, communicating with the host only through a JSON-RPC boundary over a local transport (stdio pipe or Unix domain socket / named pipe on Windows). The host process never loads plugin code in-process. This is the single decision that makes everything else — crash isolation, resource limits, permission enforcement, hot reload — tractable.

### 1.1 Extension points

The reporting tool exposes five plugin **kinds**, each with a distinct host-facing interface (§5). A single package may implement more than one kind if declared in its manifest.

| Kind | Purpose | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `data-source` | Fetch/stream raw data into the report pipeline | Salesforce connector, internal warehouse connector |
| `transform` | Shape/aggregate/enrich data between fetch and render | currency normalization, PII redaction |
| `renderer` | Turn a data frame into a visual report element | chart types, pivot tables |
| `exporter` | Serialize a finished report to an output format | PDF, XLSX, PPTX |
| `trigger` | Schedule or event-drive report runs | cron trigger, webhook trigger |

