## 0. Scope and plugin taxonomy

The host (the reporting tool) exposes five **extension points** ("contribution types"). A plugin may contribute to one or more:

| Extension point | Purpose | Runs where |
|---|---|---|
| `dataSources` | Connect to and query external data (SQL, REST, warehouse, files) | Server sandbox |
| `transforms` | Pre/post-process report data (joins, calculated fields, PII masking) | Server sandbox |
| `widgets` | Render a visualization/component inside a report | Browser sandbox (iframe) |
| `exporters` | Produce output formats (PDF, XLSX, Slack post, email digest) | Server sandbox |
| `triggers` | Schedule or event-drive report generation (cron, webhook, data-change) | Server sandbox |

All five share one registry, one manifest schema, one lifecycle, and one versioned API — only the sandbox transport differs (server-process vs. browser-iframe, §4).

