## 2. High-Level Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Host Process (Reporting Tool Core)                           │
│                                                                │
│  ┌───────────────┐   ┌────────────────┐   ┌────────────────┐ │
│  │ Plugin         │   │ Lifecycle       │   │ Host API       │ │
│  │ Registry       │──▶│ Manager         │──▶│ Services       │ │
│  │ (manifest DB,  │   │ (load/unload/   │   │ (data, UI,     │ │
│  │  resolution)   │   │  reload, health)│   │  storage, log) │ │
│  └───────────────┘   └────────┬────────┘   └───────┬────────┘ │
│                                │                     │          │
│                        IPC / RPC bridge (JSON-RPC over channel)│
│                                │                     │          │
└────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────┼─────────┘
                                  │                     │
                    ┌─────────────▼─────────┐  ┌────────▼────────┐
                    │ Sandbox: Plugin A      │  │ Sandbox: Plugin B│
                    │ (worker_thread / proc) │  │ (worker_thread)  │
                    │ capability-scoped API  │  │ capability-scoped│
                    └────────────────────────┘  └──────────────────┘
```

Each plugin runs in its own isolation boundary (§5). The host never loads plugin code in-process. All interaction crosses an RPC bridge that enforces the versioned API contract (§4) and the plugin's declared permission grants (§5.3).

