## 3. Plugin manifest schema

Every plugin ships a `plugin.json` at its bundle root, validated against this JSON Schema before anything else happens (registry rejects on failure — no partial installs).

```json
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://reporting-tool.internal/schemas/plugin-manifest-v1.json",
  "title": "Reporting Tool Plugin Manifest",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "manifestVersion", "id", "name", "version", "apiVersion",
    "entry", "contributes", "permissions"
  ],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "manifestVersion": { "const": 1 },

    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*\\.[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$",
      "description": "Namespaced, team-prefixed. e.g. 'team-growth.churn-report'. Immutable once published."
    },
    "name": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 80 },
    "version": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+(-[0-9A-Za-z-.]+)?$",
      "description": "Plugin's own SemVer, independent of apiVersion."
    },
    "description": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 500 },

    "author": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["team", "contact"],
      "properties": {
        "team": { "type": "string" },
        "contact": { "type": "string", "description": "Slack channel or email, required for incident routing." }
      }
    },

    "apiVersion": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "SemVer RANGE against the Host API contract, e.g. '^3.2.0'. Resolved at install time; see §4.",
      "pattern": "^[\\^~]?\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+$"
    },

    "entry": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Relative path to the compiled entry module implementing PluginLifecycle."
    },

    "permissions": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "Capability scopes requested. Enforced by the API gateway at call time, not just at install. See §7.2 for the full list.",
      "items": {
        "enum": [
          "data:read:reports",
          "data:read:datasources",
          "data:write:reports",
          "net:fetch:allowlisted",
          "storage:plugin-scoped",
          "schedule:register",
          "ui:contribute-widget",
          "export:register-format",
          "secrets:read:own-namespace"
        ]
      }
    },

    "dependencies": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Other plugin ids this plugin requires present & active, mapped to a SemVer range on THEIR plugin version (not apiVersion).",
      "additionalProperties": { "type": "string" }
    },

    "contributes": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Declares which extension points this plugin implements. Each must match an interface in the SDK for the declared apiVersion.",
      "properties": {
        "dataSources": { "type": "array", "items": { "$ref": "#/definitions/dataSourceContribution" } },
        "reportRenderers": { "type": "array", "items": { "$ref": "#/definitions/rendererContribution" } },
        "exportFormatters": { "type": "array", "items": { "$ref": "#/definitions/exportContribution" } },
        "widgets": { "type": "array", "items": { "$ref": "#/definitions/widgetContribution" } },
        "scheduledJobs": { "type": "array", "items": { "$ref": "#/definitions/jobContribution" } }
      },
      "minProperties": 1
    },

    "config": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "JSON Schema describing this plugin's own admin-configurable settings. Rendered as a form by the host settings UI."
    },

    "resources": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Resource ceilings enforced by the sandbox. Missing fields fall back to org-wide defaults.",
      "properties": {
        "memoryMb": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 32, "maximum": 512, "default": 128 },
        "cpuTimeMsPerCall": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 100, "maximum": 30000, "default": 5000 },
        "wallTimeMsPerCall": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 100, "maximum": 60000, "default": 10000 }
      }
    },

    "integrity": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["algorithm", "hash", "signature"],
      "description": "Filled in by the build/publish pipeline, not hand-authored. See §7.1.",
      "properties": {
        "algorithm": { "const": "sha256" },
        "hash": { "type": "string" },
        "signature": { "type": "string", "description": "Detached signature over the hash, signed by the org's plugin-publishing key." }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Example manifest:

```json
{
  "manifestVersion": 1,
  "id": "team-growth.churn-report",
  "name": "Churn Report",
  "version": "1.4.0",
  "description": "Monthly churn breakdown by cohort.",
  "author": { "team": "growth", "contact": "#team-growth" },
  "apiVersion": "^3.2.0",
  "entry": "dist/index.js",
  "permissions": ["data:read:reports", "data:read:datasources", "storage:plugin-scoped"],
  "dependencies": {},
  "contributes": {
    "reportRenderers": [
      { "id": "churn-cohort-chart", "reportTypes": ["churn"], "outputs": ["svg", "png"] }
    ],
    "scheduledJobs": [
      { "id": "monthly-churn-refresh", "cron": "0 6 1 * *", "handler": "runMonthlyRefresh" }
    ]
  },
  "resources": { "memoryMb": 128, "cpuTimeMsPerCall": 5000 },
  "integrity": { "algorithm": "sha256", "hash": "…", "signature": "…" }
}
```

**Validation rules enforced by the registry beyond JSON Schema:**
- `id` must be globally unique and, once published, its `author.team` prefix is immutable (team A can't publish under team B's namespace).
- `apiVersion` range must intersect the host's currently supported API version window (§4.3) or install is rejected with a clear "requires host API vX–Y, host provides Z" error.
- Every entry under `contributes` must reference an extension-point interface that exists in the SDK version resolved from `apiVersion`.
- `integrity.signature` must verify against the org's publishing key (§7.1) — unsigned manifests are rejected outside local dev mode.

