# Reporting Tool — Plugin Architecture

## 1. Goals / non-goals

**Goals:** 5 teams ship report types, data sources, renderers, exporters, widgets independently, without touching host code or each other's plugins. A broken/malicious plugin can't crash the host or read another plugin's data. Hot install/upgrade/rollback with no host restart. Plugins built this quarter keep working after next quarter's host releases.

**Non-goals (v1):** cross-plugin direct communication (only host-mediated composition, §8.4), external/public marketplace (internal-only registry), non-JS plugin runtimes (WASM noted as a future extension point, §6.5).

## 2. Architecture at a glance

```
plugin bundles → Plugin Registry (discovery, validation, version resolution)
                      → Registry Store (DB: installed/enabled/version state)
                      → Lifecycle Manager (state machine, hook dispatch)
                           → Sandbox Manager (spawns/kills a worker per plugin)
                                → Host API Gateway (permission checks, versioned RPC)
                                → Sandboxed Plugin Worker (isolated-vm + worker_thread,
                                  no fs/net/process, only a capability-scoped HostAPI stub)
```

Five independently-buildable pieces: **manifest schema**, **versioned API contract**, **registry**, **lifecycle manager**, **sandbox boundary**.

## 3. Plugin manifest schema

Every plugin ships `plugin.json`, validated before anything else happens (reject on failure, no partial installs):

```json
{
  "$id": "https://reporting-tool.internal/schemas/plugin-manifest-v1.json",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["manifestVersion", "id", "name", "version", "apiVersion", "entry", "contributes", "permissions"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "manifestVersion": { "const": 1 },
    "id": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*\\.[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$",
      "description": "Team-prefixed, e.g. 'team-growth.churn-report'. Immutable once published." },
    "name": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 80 },
    "version": { "type": "string", "pattern": "^\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+(-[0-9A-Za-z-.]+)?$" },
    "description": { "type": "string", "maxLength": 500 },
